Additionally, your implementation must handle a large dataset efficiently to minimize memory usage and processing time. Consider that this function will be part of a larger system with multiple dependencies, such as database access for dynamic data updates and logging for audit purposes. Ensure that your implementation accounts for potential race conditions and thread safety when interacting with shared resources.

You should also design your function to handle edge cases where input data might contain duplicate keys or extremely large values, ensuring robustness and performance under these conditions.

```cpp
std::vector<std::pair<std::string, int>> vec = {{"apple", 1}, {"banana", 2}, {"cherry", 3}};
std::pair<std::string, int> new_pair = {"date", 4};

// Insert new_pair after "banana" or at the end if "banana" is not found
