- Deleting the specified directory if it exists using a separate thread to handle potential race conditions
- Reading large output streams efficiently by reading lines instead of loading the entire stream into memory
- Catching and handling `IOException` exceptions gracefully
- Providing informative logging for debugging purposes
- Using a single-threaded executor service to manage potential race conditions when checking and deleting the directory.']

