import java.io.*;
import java.lang.reflect.InvocationTargetException;
import java.lang.ClassNotFoundException;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;

class SerializationUtils {
    private static final ConcurrentHashMap<String, Class<?>> CLASS_CACHE = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private static final ThreadLocal<ObjectOutputStream> SERIALIZATION_CONTEXT = ThreadLocal.withInitial(() -> new ObjectOutputStream(new ByteArrayOutputStream()));

    static <T> T deserializeFromByteArray(byte[] byteArray) {
        try (ObjectInputStream input = new ObjectInputStream(new ByteArrayInputStream(byteArray))) {
            Class<?> clazz = CLASS_CACHE.getOrDefault(input.readUTF(), null);
            if (clazz == null || !clazz.isAssignableFrom(getClass())) {
                throw new InvalidSerializationException("Unable to deserialize provided byte array: Unknown or invalid class.");
            }
            return (T) input.readObject();
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException | InstantiationException | IllegalAccessException | InvocationTargetException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Unable to deserialize provided byte array.", e);
        }
    }

    static void registerClassForSerialization(Class<?> clazz) {
        CLASS_CACHE.putIfAbsent(clazz.getName(), clazz);
    }
}

class InvalidSerializationException extends RuntimeException {
    public InvalidSerializationException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}
```
In this code, the `deserializeFromByteArray()` method takes a byte array and returns an object of the specified class using Java serialization. It utilizes ObjectInputStream to deserialize the given byte array. If the deserialization fails or the class of the object being deserialized is not found or does not match, it throws a custom exception `InvalidSerializationException`.

To handle different versions of classes used for serialization, the code uses a concurrent cache (`CLASS_CACHE`) to store the available classes. If a class is not found in the cache during deserialization, it will not be loaded, ensuring compatibility with different class versions.

The code also manages data integrity and consistency by using ObjectOutputStream's ByteArrayOutputStream for serialization and ObjectInputStream's ByteArrayInputStream for deserialization, which enables handling of external data sources such as databases or network communications.

For performance optimization, the code utilizes a ConcurrentHashMap (`CLASS_CACHE`) to minimize the lookup time during deserialization. This is especially beneficial when dealing with large byte arrays or frequent deserializations.

Lastly, the method integrates well with other parts of an application or third-party systems by being flexible and adaptable. The `registerClassForSerialization()` method allows registering classes for serialization on demand, making it easy to integrate new classes into the existing system.']

