The implementation ensures that each record's key does not already exist in the keys array by iterating through the keys array until finding a suitable index, using offsets to keep track of allocated indices. The function then prints the contents of the records array after allocation and initialization. Finally, it frees the memory allocated for offsets.

The arc4random_range and arc4random_uniform functions implement the ARC Four random number generator algorithm, a pseudorandom number generator that is efficient and provides good distribution without using too much CPU time.']

