The implementation is designed to work efficiently on both 32-bit and 64-bit systems. It also accounts for scenarios where input data might be large or contain outliers, handles edge cases such as empty input lists or invalid input values, and optimizes memory usage by reusing allocated memory where possible.

The code can easily be adapted to read from files or network streams instead of standard input by modifying the `read_and_initialize` function. The sorting, search, and print functions can also be used independently in your program.']

